# build output
build/
# Local sandbox: the copied L1 model + runtime session/telemetry. The pack itself stays OUT of git —
# it is a DERIVED artifact (a deterministic function of the corpus and the d256 encoder, both of which
# ARE tracked), and ~25 MB of binaries re-added on every rebuild is exactly the history bloat
# docs/repo-history-purge.md exists to undo.
sd/*
# ...but the provenance sidecar DOES go in. It is 254 bytes, and it is what lets check_pack tell a
# fresh clone "this fixture does not match this corpus" instead of passing vacuously — which is how
# the gate scored against a wrong-dimension pack for weeks without anyone being able to notice.
!sd/data/
sd/data/*
!sd/data/anima/
sd/data/anima/*
!sd/data/anima/*.prov
